# Copy to .env and edit. Used by docker-compose.yml.

# The directory that holds ALL your tagged datasets — not one dataset. Every
# folder underneath becomes selectable when creating a project, so point this at
# the library and choose the specific dataset in the UI.
#
# It is mounted read-only at /workspace/datasets, so a dataset at
#   D:\Tagged\Sub_Saharan\images\v8
# appears in the app as
#   /workspace/datasets/Sub_Saharan/images/v8
#
# Windows drives work (via /mnt/<drive> from WSL) and so do Linux paths. Reading
# training data from /mnt/* crosses the 9p bridge and is slower, which can leave
# the GPUs waiting on the dataloader — fine for scanning, worth measuring before
# a long run. Watch GPU utilisation during the first epochs.
DATASETS_HOST_ROOT=/mnt/d/Tagged

# Examples:
#   DATASETS_HOST_ROOT=/mnt/d/Tagged          all datasets on the D: drive
#   DATASETS_HOST_ROOT=/mnt/c/Users/Carl/data a folder on C:
#   DATASETS_HOST_ROOT=/srv/datasets    the Linux filesystem (fastest)

# Where prepared datasets and run outputs are written. Default to ./prepared and
# ./runs next to this file.
#
# Override them if the checkout lives on a Windows drive (Desktop, C:\, etc).
# prepared/ needs to be on the Linux filesystem to hold symlinks - on drvfs,
# symlink creation usually needs Developer Mode and otherwise falls back to
# copying, which duplicates the entire dataset.
#
# PREPARED_PATH=/srv/sparrow/prepared
# RUNS_PATH=/srv/sparrow/runs

# Annotation batches: images copied in for AI-assisted tagging, plus the XML
# written for them. Same advice as prepared/ - keep it on the Linux
# filesystem, because the review editor loads one full-size image per click.
#
# ANNOTATIONS_PATH=/srv/sparrow/annotations

# Which drives the annotation export may write to. Mounted read-write under
# /write, separately from the read-only /browse mounts used for datasets, so
# that scanning a dataset can never modify it. Set DRIVE_C / DRIVE_D if your
# drives are somewhere other than /mnt/c and /mnt/d.
#
# DRIVE_C=/mnt/c
# DRIVE_D=/mnt/d

# Optional: pin a verified torch build.
# TORCH_SPEC=torch==2.8.0 torchvision==0.23.0 torchaudio==2.8.0
